Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||03-26-2001||12:38 AM||||my car came with a viper alarm/remote entry kit installed, but the remote has long since stopped working (got pushed into a pool with keys in my pocket) hasn't been a big deal as my car has been down for a few months (spun a bearing big time about 40 miles after installing a new clutch) but the folks at cwestco.com are helping me out with a new engine, so it looks like i need to worry about the alarm. i know i can just unplug it, but i worry about my car being stolen, as my old 86se was stolen and trashed a long time back. thanks for any responses||||reg||1
Z||000001||WampusCat||03-26-2001||08:53 AM||||Any shop that installs alarms should have extra remotes and be able to code them to your system.  My car came with only one remote so I went to the local stereo/alarm dude and got a spare.<P>p.s. my alarm's an excalibur, I'm assuming that Vipers are similar.<p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
